    title: "Trump says US will find out about Iranian dirty bomb plot 'rumour'",
    summary: "Trump says US will find out about Iranian dirty bomb plot 'rumour' US President Donald Trump said on Friday that there was a \"rumour\" that Iran was building a dirty bomb. He added that if Iran was doing so, the United States would find out and stop it. CNN had reported earlier this week that US intelligence indicated Iran could be attempting to build a dirty bomb and detonate it in Washington. Iran's foreign ministry denied the allegations on Tuesday, calling them \"baseless\". A dirty bomb is far less destructive than a nuclear bomb, which relies on a fission reaction. Speaking to reporters, Trump also repeated his claim that the US has \"total control\" over the Strait of Hormuz. \"Last week, we took out record amounts of oil from the Hormuz Strait. Our navy has a blockade,\" he said. \"We have total control over the Hormuz Strait.\" \"Iran will never have a nuclear weapon, ever,\" he added. US President Donald Trump points as reporters raise their hands to ask questions during a press conference at the White House in Washington, DC, 20 November 2026 (REUTERS/Kylie Cooper)",
    preview: "Trump says US will find out about Iranian dirty bomb plot 'rumour' US President Donald Trump said on Friday that there was a \"rumour\" that Iran was building a dirty bomb. He added that if Iran was doing so, the United States would find out and stop it. CNN had reported earlier this week that US intelligence indicated Iran could be attempting to build a dirty bomb and detonate it in Washington. Iran's foreign ministry denied the allegations on Tuesday, calling them \"baseless\".",
    body: "Trump says US will find out about Iranian dirty bomb plot 'rumour' US President Donald Trump said on Friday that there was a \"rumour\" that Iran was building a dirty bomb. He added that if Iran was doing so, the United States would find out and stop it. CNN had reported earlier this week that US intelligence indicated Iran could be attempting to build a dirty bomb and detonate it in Washington. Iran's foreign ministry denied the allegations on Tuesday, calling them \"baseless\".\n\nA dirty bomb is far less destructive than a nuclear bomb, which relies on a fission reaction. Speaking to reporters, Trump also repeated his claim that the US has \"total control\" over the Strait of Hormuz. \"Last week, we took out record amounts of oil from the Hormuz Strait. Our navy has a blockade,\" he said. \"We have total control over the Hormuz Strait.\" \"Iran will never have a nuclear weapon, ever,\" he added.\n\nUS President Donald Trump points as reporters raise their hands to ask questions during a press conference at the White House in Washington, DC, 20 November 2026 (REUTERS/Kylie Cooper)",
