    summary: "Tanker catches fire after projectile strike near Strait of Hormuz - UKMTO A tanker caught fire after a projectile struck it while sailing through the Strait of Hormuz, the United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations (UKMTO) agency said on Friday. The incident occurred 8 nautical miles north of the Omani town of Khasab, UKMTO said, adding that no casualties or environmental impact were reported. Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps said shortly afterwards that an oil tanker had caught fire after hitting a mine while attempting to transit the Strait of Hormuz near Khasab, Iranian media reported. Khasab is located on Oman's Musandam Peninsula at the entrance to the Strait of Hormuz.",
