    title: "UK anthem returns to the EU stage in symbolic post-Brexit moment",
    summary: "UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham was welcomed by EU leaders in Brussels for a summit aimed at strengthening post-Brexit relations. God Save the King rang out for the first time since Brexit at the UK–EU summit.",
    preview: "British Prime Minister Andy Burnham was welcomed to Brussels on 20 November 2026 to the strains of God Save the King, the first time the UK national anthem has been played at an EU institution since Britain’s 2020 exit. European Council President António Costa and European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen welcomed the British leader before the trio posed for cameras, listened to Beethoven’s Ode to Joy and greeted their negotiating teams.",
