    title: "Houthis say 41 killed as Saudi-led coalition launches 'special operation' in Yemen",
    summary: "Houthis say 41 killed as Saudi-led coalition launches 'special operation' in Yemen Saudi-led coalition strikes on Yemen killed 41 people in the past 24 hours, the Houthis said on Friday, after the coalition attacked the Red Sea port city of Hodeidah and other targets in what it called a “special operation”. The coalition said it hit smuggling and weapons-transporting operations in Hodeidah while also carrying out attacks in Sanaa, Saada and Taiz governorates. Meanwhile, Houthis had vowed to hit Jeddah and other Saudi Red Sea ports if Hodeidah was attacked, while warning airlines that Saudi airspace was “unsafe”. They also threatened Riyadh’s financial district and a power station in Al-Shuqaiq. “We targeted operational capabilities at Hodeidah port that were used in smuggling operations and the transport of weapons and ballistic missiles,” Saudi coalition spokesman Turki al-Malki posted on X. The coalition hit “military targets” in Sanaa, including missile and drone facilities and a supply depot, he added. Two ballistic missiles were intercepted over the Jizan region near the Yemen border, he posted later, with debris falling in Al-Shuqaiq. The Houthis’ Al-Masirah television broadcast images of a damaged power station in Mokha after a coalition air raid. JUST IN: Saudi Arabia has struck Yemen's Hodeidah port, becoming the third country to attack the strategic port after the United States and Israel. In response Ansarallah warned that Jeddah, Jizan and Yanbu ports, along with Riyadh's financial district, would be targeted. https://t.co/lHCVGpfkxf — Current Report (@Currentreport1) November 20, 2026",
